"id": "irregular-aorists",
"el": "Ανώμαλοι αόριστοι",
"title": "Irregular aorists",
"span": "A2–B1",
"blurb": "The twenty or so everyday verbs whose past you simply learn by heart (είπα, είδα, ήρθα, πήγα, έφαγα, ήπια, πήρα...), with their dependent forms (να πω, να δω, να έρθω) and the idioms built on them.",
"intro": [
{
"p": "A handful of very common verbs do not follow the -σα / -ψα / -ξα patterns. They are the verbs you use most, so they come up in almost every sentence about yesterday: **Τι είπες;** \"What did you say?\", **Ήρθε ο Νίκος.** \"Nikos came.\", **Πού πήγατε;** \"Where did you go?\". Learn each one as a set of three: present, aorist, dependent form."
